Lighting:
The way I see it..  The lighting in the dungeon reflets the old days when
people used to put torches in the wall to light hallways.. and as I
recall..  Hallways wer lit up just as much as a room.

Anywayz..  I don't sompletely think this should be true..  completely lit
hallways is boring.  It would make it simple..  However.. maybe on the
first 3 Dlevels.. or whenever the dev team decides is cool, mak every
other space lit up.  That would give it a more realistic effect.  Weird,
but realistic.  

One more note on lighting..  Nethack is NOT like other DND games..  It is
a little bit modern.  One thing I HATE about NH.. is the invisibility
problems.. You can never get into a shop when invisible.  It sucks..  one
mistake with a cursaed cloak and POOF.  So what I propose is this:
Flourecent Lighting.
Why not?  Under flourecent lighting all invisible things would be visible.
 Then we could happily enter shops.  The dev team could also use it to
make other quest areas more difficult.. and to add a bit of humor to the
game.  I think it would be a great thing to add.  Oh well.



